<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Proposition <a href="/tag/43E46F" data-tag="43E46F">4.1.2.5</a>, $p$ is cofinal if and only if it is a contravariant equivalence in $(\sSet )_{/S}$. If $S$ is a Kan complex, then Proposition <a href="/tag/DC07BB" data-tag="DC07BB">3.1.5.7</a> asserts that the contravariant equivalences are precisely the weak homotopy equivalences. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
